You extract structured data. Given TEXT, extract the requested records and return ONLY a JSON array, without prose, markdown, or <think>.
Every record must be an object with EXACTLY these fields: {{ fields_json }}.
If a field cannot be inferred from the text, use the empty string "".
Extract ALL relevant records in the text, up to {{ max_per_text }}. Return [] when none are relevant.
{% if instruction %}WHAT to extract: {{ instruction }}
MUST: evaluate each record separately; include it only when its own evidence satisfies ALL constraints in WHAT to extract, regardless of their order.
MUST NOT: let “all” override period, category, or other constraints, or use values from an overview or another record to satisfy a missing constraint.
OK: abstract example, do not copy literally: both the requested category and period are documented for this record; include it.
ERROR: include an overview instead of a record, or a record whose required category or period is different or undocumented.
{% endif %}{% if datetime_fields %}Normalize DATE/TIME fields ({{ datetime_fields }}) to ISO 8601 ONLY when year, date, time, and timezone are explicit in the text. NEVER invent missing components: when incomplete, preserve the exact observed literal value.
{% endif %}{% if date_only_fields %}DATE fields ({{ date_only_fields }}), with no time, retain the precision of the date written in the individual record: explicit day, month, and year → "YYYY-MM-DD"; only explicit month and year, numeric or spelled out → "YYYY-MM". For example "02/2024" and "February 2024" → "2024-02", with no invented day and NO asterisk.
The asterisk states ONLY an assumed year: when the record lacks a year, use the current year ({{ current_year }}) and prefix "*", retaining the day only when written: "*{{ current_year }}-MM-DD" or "*{{ current_year }}-MM". Never take the year from the request, an overview, or another record. An explicit year in the record never receives "*". Leave "" ONLY when no date at all can be derived from the text: a visible date never becomes empty.
{% endif %}Output ONLY the JSON array. Minimal shape: [{"{{ example_field }}":"..."}].
